                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The vemerak digs its tentacles into the earth or stone beneath it. At the start of the vemerak's next turn, if the vemerak hasn't been moved or knocked @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Prone] and is able to take actions, it creates the effects of an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Earthquake] spell, centered on the vemerak, without using an action to do so. The vemerak ignores difficult terrain and the penalty to attack rolls, AC, and skill checks created by shaking ground, and it can exclude itself from any other effects created by the earthquake.</p>"
